  "build": "cargo +1.99.0 build --release -p esp32sim; identical workspace release profile for all arms",
  "adoption": "Keep board capability cache, active RMT mask, event-driven SPI delivery and disabled interrupt guards. Do not adopt subsequent IRQ-cache or lazy-guard candidates: paired pilots did not establish a further improvement. Remaining median C3 cost versus main is 6.1%; no claim of parity.",
  "history": "Earlier batches retain noisy and negative measurements. cpu-initial and cpu-c3-paired precede board capability caching; cpu-board-cache precedes the RMT running mask. cpu-irq-cache and cpu-lazy test the preserved rejected patches on the final C3 source. Binary and firmware hashes identify each measurement; earlier working revisions were superseded, so intermediate timing alone is not an adoption claim.",
  "privacy": "No raw process captures, application inventory or personal paths retained. Commands use caller-supplied paths, MAC is all zeroes, aggregate load is retained. Numeric samples and artifact hashes are unchanged.",
  "equivalent_c3_source_revision": "21ca035d7ed8800f9e8bffa75b25d553138b732a",
  "equivalence": "Production Rust is unchanged after the measured C3 revision; the later revision contains an added interrupt-transition test and documentation rebases."
